issue.description:
Create a richer set of visually compelling UI widgets/cards for the Personal UI gallery, building on the container-responsive gallery work from <issue id="da028771-3ce0-4ba0-83b0-227aa90b0f25" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-78/refine-gallery-with-container-responsive-nested-layout">PUI-78</issue>.

Intent:
This ticket is intentionally less prescriptive than most Personal UI tickets.

The goal is to give the worker meaningful creative freedom and test its ability to design strong UI compositions within the system, rather than implementing a narrowly specified mockup.

Owner direction:

* Fill the gallery with beautiful, polished UI widgets/cards/compositions.
* Favor strong visual variety and composition quality over strict uniformity.
* The worker may interpret what kinds of widgets/cards best showcase the design system.
* Use shadcn components where they are useful, but do not treat shadcn components as a hard constraint if a more expressive custom composition is appropriate.
* Even when custom UI is used, styling must remain driven by the Personal UI semantic token system so the results remain editable from the Workbench.
* The gallery should feel like a curated showcase of what the design system can produce, not merely a component test matrix.

Design freedom:
The worker is encouraged to explore combinations such as:

* dashboards;
* stats/metrics;
* charts/data summaries;
* profile/account surfaces;
* activity/timeline cards;
* forms/settings;
* notifications;
* commerce/finance widgets;
* media/content cards;
* lightweight productivity surfaces;
* compact utility widgets;
* other compositions that make good use of the available gallery shapes.

These examples are inspiration, not a required checklist.

Creative constraints:

* Do not hard-code a single aesthetic direction into the product architecture.
* Do not create one-off visual styling that bypasses semantic theme tokens.
* Avoid arbitrary raw colors where a semantic Personal UI token exists.
* Typography should use the accepted Heading / Body / Mono roles appropriately.
* Radius, spacing, shadows, colors, borders, and related styling should remain theme-responsive.
* Dark/light mode must remain coherent.
* Prefer existing shadcn primitives where they fit naturally.
* Custom composition/layout code is allowed when it improves the result and remains token-driven.
* Do not add a new public component/resource solely to satisfy one gallery composition unless the abstraction is genuinely reusable.

Relationship to <issue id="da028771-3ce0-4ba0-83b0-227aa90b0f25" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-78/refine-gallery-with-container-responsive-nested-layout">PUI-78</issue>:

* <issue id="da028771-3ce0-4ba0-83b0-227aa90b0f25" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-78/refine-gallery-with-container-responsive-nested-layout">PUI-78</issue> owns the responsive gallery layout architecture.
* This ticket owns the quality, variety, and visual composition of the content placed inside that gallery.
* The worker may choose which compositions best occupy narrow, wide, stacked, or nested regions once <issue id="da028771-3ce0-4ba0-83b0-227aa90b0f25" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-78/refine-gallery-with-container-responsive-nested-layout">PUI-78</issue>’s layout is available.
* Do not re-open or redesign the gallery layout architecture unless a concrete content issue exposes a real layout defect.

Quality bar:
Aim for compositions that feel intentionally designed, visually balanced, and portfolio-quality rather than generic placeholder UI.

The gallery should demonstrate:

* hierarchy;
* spacing rhythm;
* semantic color use;
* useful density;
* responsive behavior;
* varied card proportions;
* realistic UI states;
* strong light/dark rendering;
* the expressive range of the Personal UI theme system.

Avoid:

* repetitive cards that differ only by text;
* lorem-ipsum-style filler;
* excessive decorative noise;
* generic AI-generated SaaS sameness;
* hard-coded styling that does not respond to theme controls;
* visual effects that undermine accessibility or readability.

Acceptance:

* The Cards gallery contains a stronger, more visually compelling set of UI compositions.
* Compositions show meaningful visual and structural variety.
* The gallery makes good use of the available responsive region shapes from <issue id="da028771-3ce0-4ba0-83b0-227aa90b0f25" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-78/refine-gallery-with-container-responsive-nested-layout">PUI-78</issue>.
* Styling remains driven by Personal UI semantic tokens and responds correctly to Workbench edits.
* Heading / Body / Mono typography roles are used coherently.
* Light and dark themes remain visually coherent.
* Custom UI, if introduced, remains token-driven and does not bypass the theme system.
* Existing shadcn components are reused where appropriate without constraining creative composition.
* No unnecessary public resource/component expansion is introduced.
* Accessibility, containment, responsive behavior, and interaction states remain sound.
* The worker documents the main composition choices and any custom UI introduced, but should not over-document or constrain future creative changes.

Evaluation:
This ticket should be judged primarily on:

1. visual quality;
2. variety;
3. theme responsiveness;
4. usefulness as a design-system showcase;
5. clean integration with the existing Personal UI architecture.

The worker has freedom to choose the exact composition set and visual direction within these boundaries.
